---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Stop Reinventing the Meal Plan — Meaningfully Messy"
  description="One printable with two seasonal menus, front and back. Every week, pick the next four or five dinners and shop. Free from Meaningfully Messy."
>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <div class="opt-in">
      <hr class="kicker-rule" />
      <h1 id="hero-heading" class="hero-title is-compact">Stop reinventing the meal plan</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">One printable with two seasonal menus, front and back. Every week, pick the next four or five dinners and shop.</p>

      <form id="hero-form" class="opt-in-fields" novalidate>
        <div class="opt-in-field">
          <label class="sr-only" for="hero-name">First name</label>
          <input id="hero-name" name="first_name" type="text" placeholder="First name" autocomplete="given-name" />
        </div>
        <div class="opt-in-field">
          <label class="sr-only" for="hero-email">Email address</label>
          <input id="hero-email" name="email" type="email" placeholder="Email address" autocomplete="email" required />
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="cta-button is-full">Get both menus</button>
        <p class="form-note">Free instant download. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
        <p class="form-note" role="status" aria-live="polite" id="hero-status"></p>
      </form>

      <div class="success-panel" id="hero-success">
        <p class="eyebrow is-accent">Here you go</p>
        <p>Your menus are ready — print them, stick them inside a cabinet door, and start at the top.</p>
        <a class="cta-button" href="/downloads/seasonal-menus-printable.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download the printable (PDF)</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-media">
      <figure class="photo">
        <img src="/assets/images/hero.jpg" width="580" height="724" alt="A full house, mid-afternoon" />
      </figure>
      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        <p>I don't want to spend their childhood deciding what's for dinner.</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brand-truth">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div>
        <h2>With four kids under six, I didn't need more options. I needed fewer decisions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <p class="body">Meal planning used to mean starting over every Sunday. Now I keep two lists of dinners we already eat, and grocery shopping starts with a list instead of a blank page.</p>
        <p class="body is-muted">We still get variety. I'm just not reinventing it every week.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <hr class="kicker-rule" />
    <h2 class="section-title">What's inside</h2>
    <div class="cards-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-number">01</span>
        <h3>Spring &amp; summer menu</h3>
        <p>Dinners that lean toward the grill, wraps, bowls and kebabs. One column, ready to print.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-number">02</span>
        <h3>Fall &amp; winter menu</h3>
        <p>The cozy half of the year on the back of the same page: soups, chilis, casseroles and bread on the side. Flip it when the season turns.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-number">03</span>
        <h3>Checkboxes, not a calendar</h3>
        <p>Check dinners off as you eat them. At the bottom of the list, start again at the top.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-number">04</span>
        <h3>Focus on what matters</h3>
        <p>Grocery shopping starts with a list instead of a blank page, so the mental load of dinner stops taking up your week.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-compact wrap">
    <div class="about-lite">
      <figure class="avatar">
        <img src="/assets/images/portrait.jpg" width="450" height="600" alt="Portrait of Lauren smiling" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who's sending this</p>
        <p class="body-copy">I'm Lauren, a homeschool mom of four. I share the rhythms and systems that keep our full house feeling meaningful and manageable. This is one of them.</p>
        <p class="signature">Life with kids is messy. Let's make it meaningful.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-compact wrap">
    <div class="closing-cta">
      <hr class="kicker-rule is-centered" />
      <h2 class="section-title">Get both menus, free</h2>

      <form id="closing-form" class="opt-in-fields" novalidate>
        <div class="opt-in-field">
          <label class="sr-only" for="closing-email">Email address</label>
          <input id="closing-email" name="email" type="email" placeholder="Email address" autocomplete="email" required class="is-centered" />
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="cta-button is-full">Get both menus</button>
      </form>

      <div class="closing-success" id="closing-success">
        <p class="signature">Ready — go print it.</p>
        <a class="link-underline" href="/downloads/seasonal-menus-printable.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download the printable (PDF)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  function wireOptInForm(formEl: HTMLFormElement | null, statusEl: HTMLElement | null, successEl: HTMLElement | null) {
    if (!formEl) return;

    formEl.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();

      const emailInput = formEl.elements.namedItem('email') as HTMLInputElement;
      const firstNameInput = formEl.elements.namedItem('first_name') as HTMLInputElement | null;
      const email = emailInput.value.trim();
      const firstName = firstNameInput ? firstNameInput.value.trim() : '';

      if (!email) {
        if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = 'Please enter your email.';
        return;
      }

      const submitButton = formEl.querySelector('button[type="submit"]') as HTMLButtonElement;
      submitButton.disabled = true;
      if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = '';

      // Posts to our own Cloudflare Pages Function (functions/api/subscribe.js),
      // which holds the Kit API key server-side — never in this client code.
      // Fired and not awaited on purpose: the visitor still gets their PDF
      // even if this call fails or is slow — the download isn't gated on it.
      fetch('/api/subscribe', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ email, first_name: firstName }),
      }).catch((err) => {
        console.error('Subscribe request failed:', err);
      });

      // Not formEl.hidden — .opt-in-fields sets display:flex in the
      // stylesheet, which (being author CSS) overrides the browser's
      // default [hidden] { display: none } regardless of selector specificity.
      formEl.style.display = 'none';
      if (successEl) successEl.classList.add('is-visible');
    });
  }

  wireOptInForm(
    document.getElementById('hero-form') as HTMLFormElement,
    document.getElementById('hero-status'),
    document.getElementById('hero-success')
  );

  wireOptInForm(
    document.getElementById('closing-form') as HTMLFormElement,
    null,
    document.getElementById('closing-success')
  );
</script>
